        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. Suppose a raffle has 100 equally likely numbered tickets and you own tickets 1 to 10. Let $A$ be winning and $B$ be the winning ticket being numbered from 1 to 20.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac{1}{10}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nHere $P(A\\mid B)>P(A)$, so the claim is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-4-b",
