        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "False. In the same raffle, let $A$ be winning with one of your tickets numbered 1 to 10. Let $B$ be the winning ticket being numbered from 11 to 100.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=\\frac{1}{10}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nHere $P(A\\mid B)<P(A)$, so the claim is false.",
